284
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,639
I see what's going on here.

285
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,039
This meeting today

286
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,200
is just a trap set up against CEO An!

287
00:14:51,679 --> 00:14:53,200
We are all civilized people.

288
00:14:53,639 --> 00:14:55,679
Aren't we just solving the problem?

289
00:14:56,919 --> 00:14:57,960
Solving the problem, huh?

290
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:58,600
Come here!

291
00:14:58,879 --> 00:15:00,200
I'll solve the problem with you! What are you doing?

292
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:00,960
What are you doing? I think you

293
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,279
are the biggest problem!

294
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:03,799
Speak!

295
00:15:04,279 --> 00:15:05,120
Am I right?

296
00:15:05,399 --> 00:15:06,159
Stop hitting him!

297
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,120
Stop fighting!

298
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,399
Partying and drinking every single day!

299
00:15:08,399 --> 00:15:09,679
I'll kill you! Stop hitting!

300
00:15:11,519 --> 00:15:12,519
Stop hitting!

301
00:15:13,559 --> 00:15:14,600
Speak! It's all his fault!

302
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,240
Get up!

303
00:15:17,799 --> 00:15:18,559
I'll kill you!

304
00:15:21,039 --> 00:15:21,919
Get up! Get up!

305
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,399
I'm going to kill him!

306
00:15:26,919 --> 00:15:27,679
Pull him away, quick!

307
00:15:27,679 --> 00:15:28,440
Let me go!

308
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:29,960
Tell me,

309
00:15:30,039 --> 00:15:31,200
is it your fault?

310
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:31,960
Don't pull me!

311
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:37,440
A hot Americano.

312
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,200
At a time like this,

313
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,720
why aren't you anxious at all?

314
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:45,559
Cheng Yan is not cut out to run a company.

315
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:46,399
If we just leave him be,

316
00:15:46,399 --> 00:15:47,840
Valley Breeze Group will soon be ruined.

317
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,840
You must have a backup plan, right?

318
00:15:51,399 --> 00:15:52,200
Thank you.

319
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:53,679
What backup plan could I have?

320
00:15:54,759 --> 00:15:55,960
I'll just treat it as a vacation.

321
00:15:57,159 --> 00:15:58,519
Are you really giving up?

322
00:16:01,519 --> 00:16:02,480
I'm not giving up.

323
00:16:03,039 --> 00:16:05,240
I've been in the thick of it all these years,

324
00:16:05,919 --> 00:16:07,799
so there are things I can't see clearly.

325
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:11,360
Taking a break now

326
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:13,519
allows me to stand as an outsider

327
00:16:13,519 --> 00:16:15,080
and study Valley Breeze Group.

328
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,320
You can't go on like this.

329
00:16:18,159 --> 00:16:19,799
You need to relax a bit.

330
00:16:24,879 --> 00:16:25,759
Cheer up a bit.

331
00:16:25,759 --> 00:16:27,639
Maybe you'll get some different ideas.

332
00:16:28,159 --> 00:16:29,679
Let me do a happy dance for you.

333
00:16:29,919 --> 00:16:31,879
Ears, ears, smile a bit.

334
00:16:33,039 --> 00:16:34,919
Nose, nose, smile a bit.

335
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,600
Mouth, mouth, smile a bit.

336
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,639
I have to submit it tomorrow.

337
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,200
They're all smiling.

338
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:40,200
You need...

339
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:42,000
You really need to relax.

340
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,919
Maybe then you'll figure it out by tomorrow.

341
00:16:44,039 --> 00:16:46,159
Sometimes you have to learn to slow down.

342
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,879
Take an outsider's perspective

343
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
and look at it again.

344
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,919
You might find something different.

345
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,639
Ye Xiaowei changed me a lot.

346
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:55,799
It's just too bad

347
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,600
that she is forever stuck in the past.

348
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,720
She stopped in the past.

349
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,639
But your life goes on.

350
00:17:02,879 --> 00:17:04,279
It's time to move on.

351
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:14,119
I'll be at the winery for the time being.

352
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,480
Wait.

353
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:18,880
I think

354
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:20,160
you might need to see this.

355
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,279
From now on,

356
00:17:44,599 --> 00:17:46,279
as long as you work hard for me,

357
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:50,559
if I'm making a fortune,

358
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:52,960
we will

359
00:17:53,039 --> 00:17:54,279
make a fortune together.

360
00:17:58,559 --> 00:18:00,519
Thank you for believing in me, Uncle.

361
00:18:01,039 --> 00:18:03,400
I'll definitely stick with you and make a fortune.

362
00:18:10,039 --> 00:18:11,000
Then from now on, we'll

363
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,359
rely on you, CEO Yan.

364
00:18:22,599 --> 00:18:24,079
As long as you say that,

365
00:18:24,319 --> 00:18:25,319
that's enough.

366
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:30,240
They say a new boss lights a new fire.

367
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,599
I just took over the company,

368
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:33,599
and this fire

369
00:18:33,839 --> 00:18:35,319
must burn fiercely.

370
00:18:38,039 --> 00:18:39,240
Zhuge Kongming,

371
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:41,799
Zhou Gongjin,

372
00:18:42,599 --> 00:18:44,519
help me strategize.

373
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:48,119
How to boost Valley Breeze Group's profit?

374
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,200
Well, I

375
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,880
don't know much about running the company.

376
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,960
But the way I see it,

377
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,599
if we want to boost profits,

378
00:18:54,599 --> 00:18:55,880
there are only two ways.

379
00:18:56,119 --> 00:18:57,400
Either raise prices,

380
00:18:57,519 --> 00:18:58,759
or lower costs.

381
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,680
Raising prices isn't an option.

382
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,720
According to my market research,

383
00:19:04,119 --> 00:19:06,079
everyone's cutting back on spending now.

384
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:07,799
If you raise the prices,

385
00:19:07,799 --> 00:19:08,920
the customers will just run away.

386
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:12,400
Then we can only start by lowering costs.

387
00:19:12,839 --> 00:19:15,039
I can control costs on the R&D end.

388
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:16,880
Well,

389
00:19:17,599 --> 00:19:20,240
R&D is the top priority of our company.

390
00:19:20,599 --> 00:19:21,640
For years, Valley Breeze Group

391
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,559
has maintained a strong market foothold

392
00:19:23,839 --> 00:19:26,359
by continuously launching new products.

393
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,240
I'm worried that

394
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:29,079
if R&D costs are lowered,

395
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:29,960
it will affect the company...

396
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:30,599
Luoluo,

397
00:19:30,839 --> 00:19:32,599
your thinking is a bit too rigid.

398
00:19:33,039 --> 00:19:35,319
Ordinary consumers don't know that much.

399
00:19:35,559 --> 00:19:36,480
As long as it tastes good, that's enough.

400
00:19:37,839 --> 00:19:38,640
Right.

401
00:19:39,119 --> 00:19:39,920
Lin Wanmei,

402
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:41,880
haven't you

403
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:44,559
always been in touch with the lab in California?

404
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,720
Learn from them

405
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:48,440
to lower costs

406
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:50,119
and develop new products.

407
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:51,519
Okay.

408
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:52,519
CEO Yan.

409
00:20:02,039 --> 00:20:02,880
My dear niece,

410
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:05,680
Uncle needs to give you a good talking-to.

411
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,079
You need to learn to be flexible.

412
00:20:07,559 --> 00:20:09,039
The business world is a battlefield.

413
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:10,519
You have to adapt.

414
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,759
Otherwise,

415
00:20:11,799 --> 00:20:13,759
your room for advancement will be very limited.

416
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,000
Yes,

417
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:16,759
Uncle is right.

418
00:20:17,079 --> 00:20:17,799
I see that

419
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,240
Uncle is about to become

420
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,720
the chairman of Valley Breeze Group.

421
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,960
So I also prepared some documents

422
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:25,039
for you to look at.

423
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,799
Valley Breeze Group's net profit report.

424
00:20:32,039 --> 00:20:33,000
The way I see it,

425
00:20:33,039 --> 00:20:33,720
we should

426
00:20:33,759 --> 00:20:35,279
optimize production line resources,

427
00:20:35,319 --> 00:20:36,319
allocate them rationally,

428
00:20:36,839 --> 00:20:38,319
and boost overall efficiency.

429
00:20:41,559 --> 00:20:42,799
This ice wine,

430
00:20:43,319 --> 00:20:44,720
the cost is so high,

431
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,480
but the profit is so low.

432
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:47,839
It runs counter

433
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:49,240
to our strategic layout.

434
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:52,480
Perfect timing.

435
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:53,880
Send a notice down.

436
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,039
Valley Breeze Group

437
00:20:55,039 --> 00:20:56,400
will no longer produce ice wine.

438
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,359
Cut the entire production line.

439
00:20:58,359 --> 00:20:59,119
CEO Yan,

440
00:20:59,319 --> 00:21:01,279
we've already signed agreements with the fruit farmers.

441
00:21:01,279 --> 00:21:02,640
They are about to start harvesting.

442
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,480
What agreements?

443
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:06,759
They're just a bunch of powerless, poor fruit farmers.

444
00:21:07,119 --> 00:21:08,160
Just peasants.

445
00:21:09,079 --> 00:21:10,000
It's settled then.

446
00:21:10,119 --> 00:21:10,920
Yes.

447
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,480
Brilliant move, Uncle.

448
00:21:24,319 --> 00:21:26,920
In the tasting scores for the red wines,

449
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:28,799
the variance change in the second group

450
00:21:28,799 --> 00:21:30,440
is much more stable than the first group.

451
00:21:30,759 --> 00:21:32,319
Wait, I thought the meeting started on the hour.

452
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:34,039
Why is everyone here so early?

453
00:21:34,039 --> 00:21:35,039
I'm so sorry.

454
00:21:35,039 --> 00:21:36,079
There's no seat for you,

455
00:21:37,279 --> 00:21:38,359
Director Sang.

456
00:21:39,279 --> 00:21:40,400
Come sit here.

457
00:21:40,559 --> 00:21:41,519
Zhao Yue.

458
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:42,960
You stay seated.

459
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,200
Sit down.

460
00:21:46,319 --> 00:21:48,119
I can just stand for the meeting.

461
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:50,839
My apologies.

462
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,000
As for the R&D Department,

463
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
we recently adjusted our work direction.

464
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:55,599
Your innovation team

465
00:21:55,599 --> 00:21:56,920
won't be of much use, I'm afraid.

466
00:21:57,319 --> 00:21:58,279
Then again,

467
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:00,880
you've been working for so many days

468
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,599
and haven't produced any results.

469
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,920
Since your team has nothing to do,

470
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:06,240
starting tomorrow,

471
00:22:06,519 --> 00:22:07,839
you can take your team members

472
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,200
to the vineyard and prune the vines.

473
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,720
What a load of rambling nonsense.

474
00:22:13,079 --> 00:22:14,480
Aren't you just targeting me?

475
00:22:15,119 --> 00:22:16,640
Why drag others into this?

476
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:20,359
Since you care so much about your team,

477
00:22:20,799 --> 00:22:21,880
you can go by yourself.

478
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:23,279
Fine,

479
00:22:23,279 --> 00:22:24,039
Director Lin.

480
00:22:39,799 --> 00:22:40,599
Hey, mister.

481
00:22:41,319 --> 00:22:42,920
You can't prune the grapevines like this.

482
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:44,559
You need to leave some space.

483
00:22:44,559 --> 00:22:46,000
Otherwise, they'll dry out.

484
00:22:48,319 --> 00:22:49,519
Uncle An?

485
00:22:50,279 --> 00:22:51,240
Why are you here?

486
00:22:53,519 --> 00:22:55,559
I was banished here to do hard labor.

487
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:57,160
But as for you, Uncle An,

488
00:22:57,839 --> 00:22:59,839
this doesn't seem like the pampered CEO An

489
00:22:59,839 --> 00:23:00,839
would do.

490
00:23:01,799 --> 00:23:03,319
I'm not CEO An anymore.

491
00:23:05,039 --> 00:23:06,359
I'm just a fruit farmer now.

492
00:23:10,559 --> 00:23:12,319
Then I wouldn't dare trouble you.

493
00:23:12,680 --> 00:23:14,279
If you end up ruining my grapes,

494
00:23:14,279 --> 00:23:15,519
I'll be the one taking the blame.

495
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,000
Alright, alright.

496
00:23:18,799 --> 00:23:19,440
Then,

497
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:20,720
you teach me.

498
00:23:26,519 --> 00:23:27,640
I'll only teach you once.

499
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:36,119
Look.

500
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:38,119
The force you used just now was right,

501
00:23:38,279 --> 00:23:40,000
but your positioning was a bit off.

502
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,359
Here is the new bud.

503
00:23:41,599 --> 00:23:43,079
You need to keep some distance from it.

504
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,599
Otherwise, it'll dry out.

505
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:46,480
Pruning grapevines

506
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:48,759
is a very important job for a winemaker.

507
00:23:50,079 --> 00:23:51,079
Watch closely.

508
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:53,279
The pruning cut on the branch

509
00:23:53,279 --> 00:23:55,839
must be a certain distance from the bud.

510
00:23:56,079 --> 00:23:56,960
And the cut itself

511
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:58,680
should be as small as possible.

512
00:23:58,759 --> 00:24:00,640
Because if it's too close,

513
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:02,480
the bud will be drained of moisture.

514
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:03,960
It'll die of thirst.

515
00:24:04,319 --> 00:24:05,880
If the angled cut is too large,

516
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:07,680
it'll be drained of nutrients.

517
00:24:08,279 --> 00:24:09,119
It'll starve.

518
00:24:09,839 --> 00:24:10,839
Got it?

519
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:11,799
It has to be here.

520
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:12,880
Right at this spot.

521
00:24:13,599 --> 00:24:15,400
At a 45-degree angle.

522
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:17,480
Fast,

523
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,079
precise,

524
00:24:18,079 --> 00:24:18,720
and decisive.

525
00:24:20,359 --> 00:24:21,759
Now that's perfect.

526
00:24:26,799 --> 00:24:27,759
Why are you looking at me?

527
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:32,400
I just think

528
00:24:33,759 --> 00:24:34,920
you out here in the orchard

529
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:36,799
are so different from back at the Cheng family.

530
00:24:45,519 --> 00:24:46,880
If given a choice,

531
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,759
who would want to scheme every day?

532
00:24:58,759 --> 00:24:59,799
If you're willing,

533
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:03,839
you can stay here forever.

534
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:18,839
Valley Breeze Group, get the hell out!

535
00:25:18,839 --> 00:25:19,279
Come out! Get out here!

536
00:25:19,279 --> 00:25:19,880
They're causing trouble!

537
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:20,559
Pay us back!

538
00:25:21,039 --> 00:25:22,079
Give us an explanation!

539
00:25:22,079 --> 00:25:22,960
Come out! Come out!

540
00:25:23,079 --> 00:25:23,960
Get out here!

541
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:24,519
Come out!

542
00:25:24,519 --> 00:25:25,400
Valley Breeze Group, pay us back!

543
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:25,920
Get out here right now!

544
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:27,039
Get the hell out here!

545
00:25:27,119 --> 00:25:28,160
Pay us back! Brothers!

546
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:29,079
This woman...

547
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:30,519
is from Valley Breeze Group!

548
00:25:30,519 --> 00:25:31,640
She's also from the Cheng family!

549
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:32,720
Please quiet down, everyone.

550
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:34,079
Tell me what's wrong.

551
00:25:34,079 --> 00:25:35,079
I'll fix it for you, okay?

552
00:25:35,079 --> 00:25:36,079
What else is there to say?

553
00:25:36,359 --> 00:25:38,039
We work from dawn to dusk all year round

554
00:25:38,519 --> 00:25:40,200
just for those few acres of vineyards.

555
00:25:40,519 --> 00:25:42,799
They tore up the contract just like that!

556
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,720
Aren't they pushing us to a dead end?

557
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:45,599
Pay us back! - Yeah!

558
00:25:45,759 --> 00:25:46,200
Pay us back!

559
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:46,839
Folks!

560
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:48,359
Folks, listen to me.

561
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,440
Valley Breeze Group will solve this.

562
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:52,039
Please go back for now, okay?

563
00:25:52,599 --> 00:25:53,559
Give it a rest!

564
00:25:53,799 --> 00:25:55,160
She's just trying to stall

565
00:25:55,359 --> 00:25:56,240
to fool us! - Right!

566
00:25:56,240 --> 00:25:57,400
Don't listen to her nonsense!

567
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,400
She just looks down on us fruit farmers.

568
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,160
Beat her!

569
00:26:00,519 --> 00:26:01,480
I'll beat you to death!

570
00:26:01,480 --> 00:26:02,039
Beat her!

571
00:26:02,079 --> 00:26:02,759
